                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fdd94829-0124-3e40-9c5e-f139ce172b8c",
                        "entry_id": "5de9d3bc-c6d7-3dc1-86ab-fd301f413d07",
                        "glosses": [
                            "eine Frostaufwölbung aus Torf und Eis"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04893d37-ee2d-45e7-bc94-6662ecfbf4f9",
                                "sense_id": "fdd94829-0124-3e40-9c5e-f139ce172b8c",
                                "text": "„[Der Pals ist eine] beträchtliche Frostaufwölbung mit einem Torfmantel, der einen durch Frost deformierten Kern aus dauernd gefrorenen Schichten schlammigen oder torfigen Bodens umhüllt.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ded27cd7-0a91-4af5-b17e-81b9450fff8a",
                                "sense_id": "fdd94829-0124-3e40-9c5e-f139ce172b8c",
                                "text": "HÄLLEN's Theorie, dass der Pals in dem Moor so zu sagen schwimmt und daher aufgehoben wird, ist wohl nicht haltbar."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e8f2972-946d-41dd-aaa6-86ba52a2b680",
                                "sense_id": "fdd94829-0124-3e40-9c5e-f139ce172b8c",
                                "text": "Grigoriew, writing in German, used the terms 'Torf-Erdhugel' (peat-earth mounds, 2-6 m high) and 'Hocker' (knobs, up to 1 m … 153-157), 'bugor pucheniya' is a frost mound, and 'bugor torfyanoy' (or 'bugristye torfyaniki' — P'yavchenko, 1955) is a peat mound or palsa. Fyodorov and Ivanov (1974) cite 'bugor pucheniya' as referring to a palsa ('pals') but also used the term in explaining the term pingo."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30d4319b-90b1-4559-9e13-8d4b2ea0fe13",
                                "sense_id": "fdd94829-0124-3e40-9c5e-f139ce172b8c",
                                "text": "Je nach örtlichem Vorkommen in den Permafrostgebieten der Erde werden sie Pingo, Hydrolaccolith, Bugor, Bulgunnjakh und Pals genannt."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9e13c6a3-09b5-4e0c-99f5-b63238105d4e",
                        "source_entry_id": "5de9d3bc-c6d7-3dc1-86ab-fd301f413d07",
                        "source_sense_id": "fdd94829-0124-3e40-9c5e-f139ce172b8c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Geologie: eine Frostaufwölbung aus Torf und Eis",
                        "target_lang_word": "palsa",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "palsa",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d6ec744-88a6-3ac9-9270-fc3cecf6a420",
                                        "entry_id": "f88334ba-8579-3e0a-8117-7533ddbf0621",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hummock rising out of a bog with a core of ice; similar in appearance to a pingo but due to different structure palsas cannot grow as big as pingos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6441ceb4-0501-4789-9352-f2a2c62e9d92",
                                                "sense_id": "1d6ec744-88a6-3ac9-9270-fc3cecf6a420",
                                                "text": "Peat plateaux are larger landforms formed by the coalescence of palsas. String bogs, also called patterned fens, occur in muskeg. They are alternations of thin, string-like strips or ridges of peat, mainly Sphagnum moss, which may[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a54f0d57-43f0-45b6-bd2b-90a55d9a88af",
                                                "sense_id": "1d6ec744-88a6-3ac9-9270-fc3cecf6a420",
                                                "text": "These basin bogs are generally associated with Picea mariana or are treeless. Species in these wetlands are similar to those found in other palsas in Canada."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
